  "note": "Twelve operations are BUILT; the continuity path remainder stays PROPOSED. Per-operation standing replaces the former built_operations list. Every BUILT operation checks the authority contracts/capability-offices.json declares for it: the nine that declared one and checked none were guarded on Bdo's ruling of 2026-08-25, so live_matching_grant and NO_LIVE_GRANT are declared on each. Every operation that names a record also checks the record belongs to this node - a grant bound to its minting node stops a permit crossing, not a node reading another node's records under a permit of its own - so local_node_record is declared wherever a record is named by id. FOREIGN_NODE_RECORD is declared only on the three that check the node after the caller has shown a grant; the rest read the record to find their grant's scope, so they answer a foreign record exactly as they answer a missing one and return UNKNOWN_RECORD, which is not a console refusal code but the absent-record error every by-id read raises. Four operations that have enforced authority since before 2026-08-25 never declared NO_LIVE_GRANT, and PIN_INCOMPLETE, SESSION_CLOSED, THREAD_ARCHIVED and CLAIM_WITHOUT_PROPOSAL were raised without appearing in local_refusals at all, so a caller matching on reason_code had no declared name for refusals it could receive. Declared 2026-08-25. scripts/sovkernel/manifests.py checks that a declared refusal is known and never that a produced one is declared, so nothing catches this class; that gap is reported, not closed here."
